  "reasoning": [
    "Integrated module fully read. Complete unshared bodies are decoded synchronously from a local view. Shared-backed or incomplete bodies keep the owned-copy path. On fatal UTF-8 or JSON failure an owned body snapshot is installed before rethrow. Header/finish/error behavior remains as independently reviewed.",
    "Frozen baseline is a self-contained test fixture with node:util import and the original message bound. Permanent tests import production and this fixture by relative source paths. Memory tests spawn process.execPath against the source-tree probe; none requires ignored build evidence. New files remain untracked in this checkout and must be included when committing, but are not ignored.",
    "Allocation test constructs decoder and input before synchronous instrumentation, so it measures temporary body work without conflating constructor header allocation or framing. Baseline proves allocation/copy counters are active. Coalesced scalar/Unicode messages prove offset progress. Every split uses offset unshared/shared Uint8Array views. Fragmented/shared checks assert owned body bytes. Malformed JSON and fatal UTF-8 repair tests distinguish copying from retention of caller views and compare follow-up pushes, empty input, invalid input and finish.",
    "Buffer.alloc/Buffer.prototype.set in measure and Buffer.concat/Buffer.prototype.set in decodeRound are captured before patching and restored in finally. No await or externally supplied callback occurs while these patches are installed. Test callbacks are synchronous; GC tests use separate child processes.",
    "GC probe uses one module-scope decoder reachable from decodeRound, a round-local body/frame, scalar observation rows, then a setImmediate turn and two GCs after decodeRound returns. The baseline sample excludes the already allocated 4-byte decoder header. Successful JSON reply strings do not intentionally retain caller array buffers. Direct negative controls prove that retaining either completed input or assembled body exceeds the 256 KiB threshold on both pinned runtimes, addressing decoder-liveness concern with observed evidence.",
    "Local staging FILES and BASELINES read without executing migration/staging. All 29 checksum entries validated, all 27 copied source files byte-compared, all ten after hashes match packet resources/current sources and their before pins match sourceChanges.after in the sole authorized cached PC plan. All eleven host hashes match current modules including protocol. No PC or compiled resource tree access.",
    "Prior independent review accepted unchanged candidate with documented excluded fabricated intrinsic/subarray/OOM behavior. Its large corpus and timing work were not repeated. Parent integration and packet JSON reports were read; prior review and stdio evidence were structurally inspected. Historical stdio pair is correctness evidence only, with uninstrumented input chunk distribution."
  ],
